Follow `RULES.md` in the repo root. The operative set is the section **Current Ericsson report — v34**. Later sections are history. Where they disagree, v34 wins. The workbook sheet `Method` carries the same Excel and chart-page rules.

This repo is the Ericsson report. The published files are `FEGE_Choked_Flat_Sites_Ericsson_v34.xlsx` and `FEGE_Choked_Flat_Sites_Ericsson_v34_Charts.html`. The same rules are written on the workbook sheet `Method`.

v34 in short:

- Peak-touch on `Max DL Capacity Usage (Mbps)` only. UL is never used. Window 11–13 Oct 2026. Guards: at least 24 samples and Peak at least 20 Mbit/s.
- Site Name = `LEFT(ERBS, 7)`, `LEFT(NodeId, 7)`, or `LEFT(EUtranCell Id, 7)`. `ERBS Id` means `ERBS`.
- Site license is the sum of `dlBbCapacityNet`. Site-hour Max DL is the sum of the ERBS hours. CGPTA90 license is 525. CGLHG01 license is 1200.
- Two dashboards and two lists: `1. Site List_ERBS` and `1. Site List_SiteLevel`. Same three categories: Tx Flat/Chocked, Peak Touch, License usage. Spelling **Chocked** is intentional.
- TP Range excludes L900. An L09-only name has a blank TP Range, not zeros. Band columns still show L09. OSS throughput, PRB, volume, and users still drop L900.
- GeoPlot draws one physical site when any ERBS is an issue or the site-level dashboard lists it. The grade is the worst display severity. Medium is drawn as Moderate. A license-only site keeps its license grade.
- Sheet `6. Missing FEG Port` is not written. `7. Immediate actions` is the site list only, BH Flag 1H only, first match wins.
- Ten non-issue sites sit at the bottom of both lists for Excel chart comparison. They are not on the Dashboard, GeoPlot issue set, Hourly KPI, Immediate actions, or the HTML page.
- The chart page has two tabs, ERBS and SiteLevel. It is the v28 page renamed to v30. Do not rebuild it unless asked.

Read uploaded files from the name. `OSS` means OSS KPI. `FEG` or `FEGE` means the FEG port KPI. A physical-site or site-database name means geo, Tech, and Site Type. A thana name means the GeoPlot thana list. Dates, V1/V2, and part numbers say how to combine files. They do not change what the file is.

OSS and FEG use the same combine order, kept as separate finals: for each date, merge V1 part1+part2, merge V2 part1+part2, then merge V1+V2. DHAPT35 and DHAPT48 are the shape pattern, not a name filter.

Do not use Tx Total BW to list or grade a site. Do not read the old site-level OSS RAR. Skip the Comparison sheet until a previous-window FEG file is provided. Do not treat `rules/V14_LOGIC.md` as this report. That file is the NCCD / Huawei baseline.
